{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F5HhE4mpMASnNBMpt4G9qU","type":"tool_result","content":"role: Deep Review Loop Manager\npurpose: Iterative code/spec review with convergence detection across review dimensions\naction: Run deep-review loop from initialization through synthesis\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: iterative_loop\n  workflow_compliance: MANDATORY\n  workflow_execution: autonomous\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: progressive_review_state\n  validation: convergence_detection\n\noperating_principles:\n  core: \"Fresh context per iteration + externalized state = no context degradation\"\n  approach: \"Dispatch focused review agent per dimension, evaluate convergence, repeat or stop\"\n  mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Review target is READ-ONLY.\"\n\nexecution_mode:\n  source: \"$ARGUMENTS\"\n  values: [auto, confirm]\n  default: confirm\n  rule: \"Every step, executor branch and flag in this file runs in both modes. Under confirm, also execute every block marked applies_to: confirm at the place that carries it, and apply the mode_overrides.confirm wording. Under auto, skip every block marked applies_to: confirm and keep the autonomous wording of this file.\"\nmode_overrides:\n  confirm:\n    purpose: \"Iterative code/spec review with convergence detection and user approval gates\"\n    action: \"Run deep-review loop with user confirmation at each phase transition\"\n    workflow_execution: \"interactive\"\n    approvals: \"multi_gate\"\n    approach: \"Dispatch focused review agent per dimension, show results, get approval, repeat or stop\"\n    mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Pause for user at each gate. Review target is READ-ONLY.\"\n    phase_loop_purpose: \"Dispatch review agent iterations with approval at each step\"\n    lock_not_acquired: \"If acquired=false, stop and present recovery choices: another deep-review run already holds this packet.\"\n    agent_dispatch_timeout: \"Retry once with reduced scope. If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and show to user for decision.\"\n    continuity_save_failure: \"Preserve the review packet in review/ as backup. Inform user.\"\n    rules_always: [pause_at_approval_gates, present_clear_options_at_each_gate]\n    rules_never: [proceed_past_approval_gate_without_user_response, auto_approve_on_behalf_of_user]\n\nuser_inputs:\n  review_target: \"[REVIEW_TARGET] - What to review. REQUIRED.\"\n  review_target_type: \"[spec-folder|skill|agent|track|files] - Target type for scope derivation. REQUIRED.\"\n  review_dimensions: \"[all|correctness,security,traceability,maintainability|custom names] - Dimensions to check. The four canonical dimensions are correctness, security, traceability and maintainability; any other name is a custom dimension, reviewed after the canonical four in configured order. A single-executor run applies the list; a fan-out run binds all in every lineage, so a subset or a custom name is not applied there. Default: all.\"\n  review_focus: \"[optional free text] - Operator review focus that every iteration covers in addition to its dimension. Default: empty, which leaves the prompt unchanged.\"\n  spec_folder: \"[SPEC_FOLDER] - Spec folder path for state files. REQUIRED.\"\n  session_id: \"[SESSION_ID] - Optional caller-supplied session id for fan-out lineages. Default: timestamp.\"\n  lineage_mode: \"[auto|resume|restart|completed-continue] - Session lifecycle intent. Default: auto. The runtime persists lineage events for `resume` (same sessionId, no archive), `restart` (new sessionId, generation+1, prior review/ archived) and `completed-continue` (from --extend=N: a completed run extended in place by N iterations, same sessionId and generation). `fork` is not accepted. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches.\"\n  extend: \"[EXTEND] - Positive integer N from --extend=N. Sets lineage_mode to completed-continue and adds N iterations to a completed run. Default: unset.\"\n  extend_minutes: \"[EXTEND_MINUTES] - Positive integer M from --extend-minutes=M, the minutes an extension adds to the later of the prior maxDurationMinutes and the minutes already elapsed since createdAt. Only valid with --extend. Default: unset, which adds the prior maxDurationMinutes, and a run with no duration budget keeps none.\"\n  max_iterations: 7\n  max_iterations_source: \"[default|flag|marker|setup|matrix] - Where max_iterations came from: default when no --max-iterations flag, maxIterations marker, setup answer or single-lineage matrix iterations value set it. A setup binding only, never written to the config. Default: default.\"\n  convergence_threshold: 0.10\n  convergence_mode: \"[default|off|sliding-window|divergent] - Convergence policy modifier. Default: default.\"\n  depth_mode: \"[default|expansive] - Opt-in frontier growth. expansive seeds depth-1 sub-target nodes, admits leaf frontier_proposal rows and vetoes a review stop candidate while nodes stay open. Default: default.\"\n  frontier_max_depth: \"[FRONTIER_MAX_DEPTH] - Positive integer N from --frontier-max-depth=N, written to expansiveDepth.maxDepth: the deepest level the frontier may grow to. Only valid with --depth-mode=expansive. Default: unset, which keeps 3.\"\n  frontier_max_nodes: \"[FRONTIER_MAX_NODES] - Positive integer N from --frontier-max-nodes=N, written to expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes: the run-wide frontier node cap. Only valid with --depth-mode=expansive. Default: unset, which keeps null, so the cap derives as half the iteration budget.\"\n  stop_policy: \"[convergence|max-iterations] - Stop behavior. Default: convergence. max-iterations treats convergence as telemetry until the hard iteration ceiling.\"\n  dry_run: \"[DRY_RUN] - Boolean pre-flight flag. Default: false.\"\n  lineage_timeout_hours: \"[LINEAGE_TIMEOUT_HOURS] - Optional per-lineage wall-clock ceiling in hours for fan-out runs, at most 4. Default: unset, which keeps the 4 hour ceiling.\"\n  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n\ndry_run_control:\n  enabled_when: \"dry_run == true\"\n  default: false\n  modes: [auto, confirm]\n  purpose: \"Run safe setup and read-only inspection, then stop before side effects.\"\n  safe_operations:\n    - \"Resolve setup inputs and artifact roots.\"\n    - \"Read current state, strategy, focus, and convergence signals.\"\n    - \"Render the next prompt to terminal preview without writing prompt files.\"\n    - \"Print each fan-out lineage's command with fanout-run.cjs --preview, which builds the commands and writes nothing.\"\n  forbidden_operations:\n    - \"Executor dispatch.\"\n    - \"Persistent state, queue, lock, git index, memory, or graph mutation.\"\n    - \"Reducer refresh or generated artifact writes.\"\n    - \"Child-lineage spawn.\"\n  event_policy:\n    event_name: dry_run_halt\n    sink: \"terminal JSONL preview only; never append to {state_paths.state_log}\"\n    required_fields: [type, event, mode, boundary, step, timestamp]\n    optional_fields: [run, sessionId, generation, detail]\n    default_halt_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"dry_run_halt\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"boundary\":\"{dry_run_boundary}\",\"step\":\"{step_name}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n    preview_only: \"A step or branch marked dry_run_event_policy: preview-only still runs its read and classify work. It prints the event it would append as a terminal JSONL preview line and appends nothing.\"\n  halt_hook_rule: \"Before executing any command, dispatch, edit, output, template write, append_to_jsonl, append_jsonl, log_event, mcp_tool, write, or git-index mutation in a step tagged with dry_run_boundary, emit event_policy.default_halt_event with that step's name and boundary to the terminal and halt; at step_fanout_spawn print the dry_run_halt the fan-out preview returned instead, when it returned one. This holds in both execution modes.\"\n  boundary_labels:\n    child_spawn: \"child-spawn\"\n    state_mutation: \"state-mutation\"\n    dispatch: \"dispatch\"\n    reducer_refresh: \"reducer-refresh\"\n\ncontext_loading:\n  trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n  purpose: \"Load prior review context for the target and buffer it until strategy.md exists\"\n  retrieval:\n    mechanism: \"continuity-ladder-then-ripgrep\"\n    note: \"File reads only, apart from the temporary pattern file below. Nothing here needs a running daemon, and every step is reproducible by hand.\"\n    ladder:\n      - \"{spec_folder}/handover.md when present\"\n      - \"the _memory.continuity frontmatter block in {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md\"\n      - \"the packet's canonical spec docs, spec.md and decision-record.md, for what the first two steps leave open\"\n    pattern_file: \"Run `mktemp -d` and bind context_pattern_file to pattern.txt inside the directory it prints. Write {review_target} into that new file with the file-write tool, never through a shell, with every line break collapsed to one space, then run free_text_recipe and remove the directory. Inside a shell argument a backtick, $() or quote in the target would be expanded or end the argument. The one-line rule keeps the target one fixed-string phrase: ripgrep reads a pattern file one pattern per line, so a second line would widen the search to either line, and a blank line is an empty pattern that matches every line.\"\n    free_text_recipe: \"rg --no-config --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case -C 2 --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/z_archive/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' -f '{context_pattern_file}' -- specs .skilled\"\n    recipe_contract: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md\"\n    exit_status: \"0 is a hit set, 1 is a clean no-hit, 2 or higher is a failure that must be surfaced instead of reported as no-hit\"\n    ranking: \"Ripgrep does not rank. Order the hits caller-side with the tuple in retrieval-conventions.md section 5.\"\n  when_to_skip: [\"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n  behavior:\n    if_context_found: \"Store full results as prior_context plus a concise prior_context_summary; inject after strategy.md is created.\"\n    if_no_context: \"Set prior_context and prior_context_summary to 'None' and continue.\"\n\nskill_reference:\n  skill: system-deep-loop\n  skill_md: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\n  references:\n    loop_protocol: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\n    state_format: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md\n    convergence: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n  templates:\n    config: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n    strategy: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n\nagent_config:\n  agent: deep-review\n  agent_file: \".skilled/agents/deep-review.md\"\n  mode: subagent\n  model: opus\n  leaf_only: true\n  tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n  mcp_servers: []\n\nstate_write_protocol:\n  mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n  applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n  refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write. Exit 1 on a row that is still routed through the gateway is a workflow defect and halts; the pinned_bookkeeping rows are recorded through bookkeeping_log and are never routed.\"\n  pinned_bookkeeping:\n    events: [config_warning, lock_released, pivot_confirm_accepted, manualStop, pivot_override_accepted, maxDurationReached]\n    directive: \"bookkeeping_log\"\n    handling: \"These rows are workflow bookkeeping that the review ledger schema pins to the legacy path: they have no lossless review-event target, so the gateway would refuse them with exit 1 and write nothing. They are never sent to the gateway. The step prints the row in its log line and continues; none of them is a halt condition.\"\n  contract: |\n    The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The gateway\n    authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it behind the\n    ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0 means the\n    record is durable in the ledger and the refreshed state_log carries it. Exit 2 means it was\n    refused, and the refusal names the check that failed.\n\n    Writing state_log directly bypasses ordering, authorization, and the receipt. Two writers\n    can then interleave with no shared ordering, and a record nobody authorized carries no\n    receipt, so a later reader cannot tell an accepted record from an invented one. A refusal\n    is a halt, never a reason to write the file directly.\n\n    There is no direct-append exception. state_log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from\n    the ledger, so a row written beside it is dropped by the next refresh: the migration\n    marker, the recovery baseline, the iteration-error row and the claim-adjudication gate\n    row are canonical ledger events like every other record.\n\nstate_paths:\n  packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n  local_packet_dir: \"{spec_folder}/review\"\n  legacy_root_report: \"{spec_folder}/review-report.md\"\n  config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n  state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n  findings_registry: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n  strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n  dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n  pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n  lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review.lock\"\n  prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n  iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n  iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n  delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n  delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n  review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n  resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n  archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n\n\ngate_defaults:\n  after_gate_refresh_lock:\n    action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately after the operator response\"\n    command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n    on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet, so run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n\nworkflow:\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-1:\ntotal 88\ndrwx------@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 24 05:44 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 michelkerkmeester  staff    192 Nov 24 05:43 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 24 05:43 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:43 containment\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-audit-ledger\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff    475 Nov 24 05:43 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 locks-and-fencing-v1\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  40598 Nov 24 05:43 review-scope-files.txt\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-2:\ntotal 88\ndrwx------@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 24 05:44 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 michelkerkmeester  staff    192 Nov 24 05:43 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 24 05:43 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 containment\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-audit-ledger\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff    475 Nov 24 05:43 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 locks-and-fencing-v1\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  40598 Nov 24 05:43 review-scope-files.txt\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-3:\ntotal 88\ndrwx------@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 24 05:44 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 michelkerkmeester  staff    192 Nov 24 05:43 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 24 05:43 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 containment\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-audit-ledger\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff    475 Nov 24 05:43 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 locks-and-fencing-v1\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  40598 Nov 24 05:43 review-scope-files.txt\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-4:\ntotal 88\ndrwx------@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 24 05:44 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 michelkerkmeester  staff    192 Nov 24 05:43 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 24 05:43 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 containment\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-audit-ledger\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff    475 Nov 24 05:43 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 locks-and-fencing-v1\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  40598 Nov 24 05:43 review-scope-files.txt\n{\"executors\":[{\"kind\":\"cli-claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"reasoningEffort\":\"medium\",\"configDir\":\"~/.claude-account2\",\"sandboxMode\":\"danger-full-access\",\"label\":\"opus\",\"count\":4}],\"concurrency\":4}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:44:46.914Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"role: Deep Review Loop Manager\npurpose: Iterative code/spec review with convergence detection across review dimensions\naction: Run deep-review loop from initialization through synthesis\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: iterative_loop\n  workflow_compliance: MANDATORY\n  workflow_execution: autonomous\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: progressive_review_state\n  validation: convergence_detection\n\noperating_principles:\n  core: \"Fresh context per iteration + externalized state = no context degradation\"\n  approach: \"Dispatch focused review agent per dimension, evaluate convergence, repeat or stop\"\n  mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Review target is READ-ONLY.\"\n\nexecution_mode:\n  source: \"$ARGUMENTS\"\n  values: [auto, confirm]\n  default: confirm\n  rule: \"Every step, executor branch and flag in this file runs in both modes. Under confirm, also execute every block marked applies_to: confirm at the place that carries it, and apply the mode_overrides.confirm wording. Under auto, skip every block marked applies_to: confirm and keep the autonomous wording of this file.\"\nmode_overrides:\n  confirm:\n    purpose: \"Iterative code/spec review with convergence detection and user approval gates\"\n    action: \"Run deep-review loop with user confirmation at each phase transition\"\n    workflow_execution: \"interactive\"\n    approvals: \"multi_gate\"\n    approach: \"Dispatch focused review agent per dimension, show results, get approval, repeat or stop\"\n    mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Pause for user at each gate. Review target is READ-ONLY.\"\n    phase_loop_purpose: \"Dispatch review agent iterations with approval at each step\"\n    lock_not_acquired: \"If acquired=false, stop and present recovery choices: another deep-review run already holds this packet.\"\n    agent_dispatch_timeout: \"Retry once with reduced scope. If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and show to user for decision.\"\n    continuity_save_failure: \"Preserve the review packet in review/ as backup. Inform user.\"\n    rules_always: [pause_at_approval_gates, present_clear_options_at_each_gate]\n    rules_never: [proceed_past_approval_gate_without_user_response, auto_approve_on_behalf_of_user]\n\nuser_inputs:\n  review_target: \"[REVIEW_TARGET] - What to review. REQUIRED.\"\n  review_target_type: \"[spec-folder|skill|agent|track|files] - Target type for scope derivation. REQUIRED.\"\n  review_dimensions: \"[all|correctness,security,traceability,maintainability|custom names] - Dimensions to check. The four canonical dimensions are correctness, security, traceability and maintainability; any other name is a custom dimension, reviewed after the canonical four in configured order. A single-executor run applies the list; a fan-out run binds all in every lineage, so a subset or a custom name is not applied there. Default: all.\"\n  review_focus: \"[optional free text] - Operator review focus that every iteration covers in addition to its dimension. Default: empty, which leaves the prompt unchanged.\"\n  spec_folder: \"[SPEC_FOLDER] - Spec folder path for state files. REQUIRED.\"\n  session_id: \"[SESSION_ID] - Optional caller-supplied session id for fan-out lineages. Default: timestamp.\"\n  lineage_mode: \"[auto|resume|restart|completed-continue] - Session lifecycle intent. Default: auto. The runtime persists lineage events for `resume` (same sessionId, no archive), `restart` (new sessionId, generation+1, prior review/ archived) and `completed-continue` (from --extend=N: a completed run extended in place by N iterations, same sessionId and generation). `fork` is not accepted. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches.\"\n  extend: \"[EXTEND] - Positive integer N from --extend=N. Sets lineage_mode to completed-continue and adds N iterations to a completed run. Default: unset.\"\n  extend_minutes: \"[EXTEND_MINUTES] - Positive integer M from --extend-minutes=M, the minutes an extension adds to the later of the prior maxDurationMinutes and the minutes already elapsed since createdAt. Only valid with --extend. Default: unset, which adds the prior maxDurationMinutes, and a run with no duration budget keeps none.\"\n  max_iterations: 7\n  max_iterations_source: \"[default|flag|marker|setup|matrix] - Where max_iterations came from: default when no --max-iterations flag, maxIterations marker, setup answer or single-lineage matrix iterations value set it. A setup binding only, never written to the config. Default: default.\"\n  convergence_threshold: 0.10\n  convergence_mode: \"[default|off|sliding-window|divergent] - Convergence policy modifier. Default: default.\"\n  depth_mode: \"[default|expansive] - Opt-in frontier growth. expansive seeds depth-1 sub-target nodes, admits leaf frontier_proposal rows and vetoes a review stop candidate while nodes stay open. Default: default.\"\n  frontier_max_depth: \"[FRONTIER_MAX_DEPTH] - Positive integer N from --frontier-max-depth=N, written to expansiveDepth.maxDepth: the deepest level the frontier may grow to. Only valid with --depth-mode=expansive. Default: unset, which keeps 3.\"\n  frontier_max_nodes: \"[FRONTIER_MAX_NODES] - Positive integer N from --frontier-max-nodes=N, written to expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes: the run-wide frontier node cap. Only valid with --depth-mode=expansive. Default: unset, which keeps null, so the cap derives as half the iteration budget.\"\n  stop_policy: \"[convergence|max-iterations] - Stop behavior. Default: convergence. max-iterations treats convergence as telemetry until the hard iteration ceiling.\"\n  dry_run: \"[DRY_RUN] - Boolean pre-flight flag. Default: false.\"\n  lineage_timeout_hours: \"[LINEAGE_TIMEOUT_HOURS] - Optional per-lineage wall-clock ceiling in hours for fan-out runs, at most 4. Default: unset, which keeps the 4 hour ceiling.\"\n  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n\ndry_run_control:\n  enabled_when: \"dry_run == true\"\n  default: false\n  modes: [auto, confirm]\n  purpose: \"Run safe setup and read-only inspection, then stop before side effects.\"\n  safe_operations:\n    - \"Resolve setup inputs and artifact roots.\"\n    - \"Read current state, strategy, focus, and convergence signals.\"\n    - \"Render the next prompt to terminal preview without writing prompt files.\"\n    - \"Print each fan-out lineage's command with fanout-run.cjs --preview, which builds the commands and writes nothing.\"\n  forbidden_operations:\n    - \"Executor dispatch.\"\n    - \"Persistent state, queue, lock, git index, memory, or graph mutation.\"\n    - \"Reducer refresh or generated artifact writes.\"\n    - \"Child-lineage spawn.\"\n  event_policy:\n    event_name: dry_run_halt\n    sink: \"terminal JSONL preview only; never append to {state_paths.state_log}\"\n    required_fields: [type, event, mode, boundary, step, timestamp]\n    optional_fields: [run, sessionId, generation, detail]\n    default_halt_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"dry_run_halt\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"boundary\":\"{dry_run_boundary}\",\"step\":\"{step_name}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n    preview_only: \"A step or branch marked dry_run_event_policy: preview-only still runs its read and classify work. It prints the event it would append as a terminal JSONL preview line and appends nothing.\"\n  halt_hook_rule: \"Before executing any command, dispatch, edit, output, template write, append_to_jsonl, append_jsonl, log_event, mcp_tool, write, or git-index mutation in a step tagged with dry_run_boundary, emit event_policy.default_halt_event with that step's name and boundary to the terminal and halt; at step_fanout_spawn print the dry_run_halt the fan-out preview returned instead, when it returned one. This holds in both execution modes.\"\n  boundary_labels:\n    child_spawn: \"child-spawn\"\n    state_mutation: \"state-mutation\"\n    dispatch: \"dispatch\"\n    reducer_refresh: \"reducer-refresh\"\n\ncontext_loading:\n  trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n  purpose: \"Load prior review context for the target and buffer it until strategy.md exists\"\n  retrieval:\n    mechanism: \"continuity-ladder-then-ripgrep\"\n    note: \"File reads only, apart from the temporary pattern file below. Nothing here needs a running daemon, and every step is reproducible by hand.\"\n    ladder:\n      - \"{spec_folder}/handover.md when present\"\n      - \"the _memory.continuity frontmatter block in {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md\"\n      - \"the packet's canonical spec docs, spec.md and decision-record.md, for what the first two steps leave open\"\n    pattern_file: \"Run `mktemp -d` and bind context_pattern_file to pattern.txt inside the directory it prints. Write {review_target} into that new file with the file-write tool, never through a shell, with every line break collapsed to one space, then run free_text_recipe and remove the directory. Inside a shell argument a backtick, $() or quote in the target would be expanded or end the argument. The one-line rule keeps the target one fixed-string phrase: ripgrep reads a pattern file one pattern per line, so a second line would widen the search to either line, and a blank line is an empty pattern that matches every line.\"\n    free_text_recipe: \"rg --no-config --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case -C 2 --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/z_archive/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' -f '{context_pattern_file}' -- specs .skilled\"\n    recipe_contract: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md\"\n    exit_status: \"0 is a hit set, 1 is a clean no-hit, 2 or higher is a failure that must be surfaced instead of reported as no-hit\"\n    ranking: \"Ripgrep does not rank. Order the hits caller-side with the tuple in retrieval-conventions.md section 5.\"\n  when_to_skip: [\"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n  behavior:\n    if_context_found: \"Store full results as prior_context plus a concise prior_context_summary; inject after strategy.md is created.\"\n    if_no_context: \"Set prior_context and prior_context_summary to 'None' and continue.\"\n\nskill_reference:\n  skill: system-deep-loop\n  skill_md: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\n  references:\n    loop_protocol: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\n    state_format: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md\n    convergence: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n  templates:\n    config: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n    strategy: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n\nagent_config:\n  agent: deep-review\n  agent_file: \".skilled/agents/deep-review.md\"\n  mode: subagent\n  model: opus\n  leaf_only: true\n  tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n  mcp_servers: []\n\nstate_write_protocol:\n  mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n  applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n  refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write. Exit 1 on a row that is still routed through the gateway is a workflow defect and halts; the pinned_bookkeeping rows are recorded through bookkeeping_log and are never routed.\"\n  pinned_bookkeeping:\n    events: [config_warning, lock_released, pivot_confirm_accepted, manualStop, pivot_override_accepted, maxDurationReached]\n    directive: \"bookkeeping_log\"\n    handling: \"These rows are workflow bookkeeping that the review ledger schema pins to the legacy path: they have no lossless review-event target, so the gateway would refuse them with exit 1 and write nothing. They are never sent to the gateway. The step prints the row in its log line and continues; none of them is a halt condition.\"\n  contract: |\n    The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The gateway\n    authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it behind the\n    ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0 means the\n    record is durable in the ledger and the refreshed state_log carries it. Exit 2 means it was\n    refused, and the refusal names the check that failed.\n\n    Writing state_log directly bypasses ordering, authorization, and the receipt. Two writers\n    can then interleave with no shared ordering, and a record nobody authorized carries no\n    receipt, so a later reader cannot tell an accepted record from an invented one. A refusal\n    is a halt, never a reason to write the file directly.\n\n    There is no direct-append exception. state_log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from\n    the ledger, so a row written beside it is dropped by the next refresh: the migration\n    marker, the recovery baseline, the iteration-error row and the claim-adjudication gate\n    row are canonical ledger events like every other record.\n\nstate_paths:\n  packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n  local_packet_dir: \"{spec_folder}/review\"\n  legacy_root_report: \"{spec_folder}/review-report.md\"\n  config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n  state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n  findings_registry: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n  strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n  dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n  pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n  lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review.lock\"\n  prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n  iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n  iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n  delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n  delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n  review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n  resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n  archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n\n\ngate_defaults:\n  after_gate_refresh_lock:\n    action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately after the operator response\"\n    command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n    on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet, so run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n\nworkflow:\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-1:\ntotal 88\ndrwx------@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 24 05:44 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 michelkerkmeester  staff    192 Nov 24 05:43 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 24 05:43 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:43 containment\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-audit-ledger\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff    475 Nov 24 05:43 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 locks-and-fencing-v1\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  40598 Nov 24 05:43 review-scope-files.txt\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-2:\ntotal 88\ndrwx------@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 24 05:44 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 michelkerkmeester  staff    192 Nov 24 05:43 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 24 05:43 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 containment\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-audit-ledger\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff    475 Nov 24 05:43 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 locks-and-fencing-v1\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  40598 Nov 24 05:43 review-scope-files.txt\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-3:\ntotal 88\ndrwx------@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 24 05:44 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 michelkerkmeester  staff    192 Nov 24 05:43 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 24 05:43 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 containment\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-audit-ledger\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff    475 Nov 24 05:43 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 locks-and-fencing-v1\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  40598 Nov 24 05:43 review-scope-files.txt\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-4:\ntotal 88\ndrwx------@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 24 05:44 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 michelkerkmeester  staff    192 Nov 24 05:43 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 24 05:43 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 containment\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-audit-ledger\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 24 05:44 deep-review-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff    475 Nov 24 05:43 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 24 05:44 locks-and-fencing-v1\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  40598 Nov 24 05:43 review-scope-files.txt\n{\"executors\":[{\"kind\":\"cli-claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"reasoningEffort\":\"medium\",\"configDir\":\"~/.claude-account2\",\"sandboxMode\":\"danger-full-access\",\"label\":\"opus\",\"count\":4}],\"concurrency\":4}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"unavailable":true}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01F5HhE4mpMASnNBMpt4G9qU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
