tness\", \"file\": \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/010-mcp-browser-use/lib/router.cjs:107\", \"lineage\": \"claude2\"},\n28:    {\"id\": \"R1-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P1\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/hub-router.json:98\", \"lineage\": \"vibe\"},\n29:    {\"id\": \"R2-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P1\", \"dimension\": \"security\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:46\", \"lineage\": \"vibe\"},\n30:    {\"id\": \"R4-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P1\", \"dimension\": \"maintainability\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing/README.md:9\", \"lineage\": \"vibe\"}\n32:  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\"WS1 routing correctness (C2-I1-P1-001, R1-P1-001)\", \"WS2 Bladebro teardown safety (R2-P1-001)\", \"WS3 stale routing evidence (R4-P1-001)\", \"WS4 P2 advisories\"],\n41:## 3. Active Finding Registry\n43:### P1 (required)\n47:| C2-I1-P1-001 | claude2 | correctness | `010-mcp-browser-use/lib/router.cjs:107` | `evaluateRoute` rejects when the prompt text contains \"forbidden\". Compiled routing is the hub's default and SKILL.md:62 says `reject` refuses, so a 403 Forbidden debugging request is refused. Reproduced live. | Reject on `constraints.has('forbidden')` only. Add a 403 canary that must route to `mcp-chrome-devtools`. |\n48:| R1-P1-001 | vibe | correctness | `hub-router.json:98`, `:119`; `ROUTER.md:51` | Stage two holds \"chrome live manual\" and \"core web vitals\"; stage one `INTENT_SIGNALS.CHROME_DEVTOOLS` holds neither, so a request carrying only one of them never selects the hub. | Add both phrases to `ROUTER.md:51`, or drop them from `hub-router.json`. |\n49:| R2-P1-001 | vibe | security | `mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:46` | `rm -rf ~/.local/state/blade` is unconditional. `install-and-verify.md:77` 