orts/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing--post-review/` records 7 of 7 PASS and supersedes the FAIL record.\n152:- **Downgraded and not changed:** R1-P1-001, now P2. A stage-one replay showed no misroute. \"chrome live manual\" already picks the hub (0.87), and \"core web vitals\" picks sk-code (0.90), whose `WEB_PERF` intent owns it. Declaring \"chrome live manual\" in `ROUTER.md` made an out-of-domain prompt pick the hub (0.835, none before), so the edit was reverted. Dropping both phrases from `hub-router.json` changes the policy hash and is the operator's call.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:45:37.570Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"20261121T221729Z-stopped-run2\n20261121T223122Z-claude2-stopped\n20261124T044326Z-restart\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review-archive/20261121T221729Z-stopped-run2:\ndeep-review-config.json\nlineages\nobservability-events.jsonl\norchestration-status.log\norchestration-summary.json\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review-archive/20261121T221729Z-stopped-run2/lineages:\nclaude2\nvibe\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review-archive/20261121T221729Z-stopped-run2/lineages/claude2:\ndeep-review-audit-ledger\ndeep-review-config.json\ndeep-review-dashboard.md\ndeep-review-effect-ledger\ndeep-review-findings-registry.json\ndeep-review-ledger\ndeep-review-state.jsonl\ndeep-review-strategy.md\ndeltas\ninvocation-metadata.json\niterations\nlocks-and-fencing-v1\nreview-scope-files.txt\n\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review-archive/20261124T044326Z-restart/review-report.md\n1:# Deep Review Report - mcp-browser-use parent hub (fan-out root)\n5:## 1. Executive Summary\n9:- Counts the verdict used: P0 = 0, P1 = 4, P2 = 17. These are the merged lineage counts from `fanout-merge.cjs`, passed to `review-verdict.cjs` with search debt 0 and no failed required gate.\n11:- S