{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BnuXwu7U23tW9PHGg1Wx9W","type":"tool_result","content":"bladebro-workflow {\"note\":\"Agentic branching, stealth signed-in work and caller-owned browser attachment. Tie-break order places Chrome DevTools first on debugging overlap and Aside first on deterministic signed-in overlap.\",\"keywords\":[\"agentic signed-in\",\"stealth signed-in\",\"agentic branching\",\"anti-detection browser\",\"attach to my open browser\",\"caller-owned browser\",\"browser i already have open\",\"already-open browser\"]}\naside-devtools-aliases {\"note\":\"Bare aside is kept: without it, requests such as \\\"run aside on the pricing page\\\" or \\\"open aside and log in\\\" name the tool and still defer. Stage two only runs after the advisor picks this hub, so ordinary-prose uses of the word never reach it.\",\"keywords\":[\"aside\",\"aside browser\",\"aside cli\",\"aside mcp\",\"aside repl\",\"aside daemon\",\"aside account\",\"aside devtools\",\"mcp-aside-devtools\"]}\n== attach to my own chrome and finish the checkout\nroute single mcp-chrome-devtools\n== use my signed-in chrome to fill the form in aside\nroute orderedBundle mcp-chrome-devtools,mcp-aside-devtools\n== in my logged in chrome, work out how to finish this signup\nroute single mcp-chrome-devtools\n22:Routing has two stages. `hub-router.json` scores the request and selects one workflow mode, an ordered bundle, or a defer outcome, and `mode-registry.json` maps that mode to its packet folder. This file then picks the leaves inside the selected packet. It never re-decides the mode.\n30:Generic browser-automation phrasing names no tool, so it fires no intent here and the hub defers. That covers \"browser automation\", \"agentic browser\" and \"ai browser automation\": a bare agentic request belongs to neither Aside nor Bladebro.\n45:# a request that fires no intent takes the hub's defer fallback.\n51:    \"CHROME_DEVTOOLS\":  {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"chrome devtools\", \"open devtools\", \"via devtools\", \"use devtools\", \"in devtools\", \"devtools console\", \"browser debug\", \"bdg\", \"cdp\", \"chrome-devtools\", \"mcp-chrome-devtools\", \"inspect the dom\", \"screenshot capture\", \"console errors\", \"network requests\", \"har export\", \"export a har\", \"har file\", \"cdp domain\", \"capture browser screenshots\", \"chrome_devtools_live\", \"chrome devtools live\", \"remote debugging\", \"chrome autoconnect\", \"my own chrome\", \"signed-in chrome\", \"logged in chrome\"]},\n84:- No keyword match is the hub's defer fallback: confirm the browser mode before loading anything.\n105:> Follow the returned decision: `route` uses its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask for disambiguation, and `reject` refuses. On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the registry routing in `hub-router.json`. Set `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=0` to force legacy routing for every hub.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:47:37.911Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"bladebro-workflow {\"note\":\"Agentic branching, stealth signed-in work and caller-owned browser attachment. Tie-break order places Chrome DevTools first on debugging overlap and Aside first on deterministic signed-in overlap.\",\"keywords\":[\"agentic signed-in\",\"stealth signed-in\",\"agentic branching\",\"anti-detection browser\",\"attach to my open browser\",\"caller-owned browser\",\"browser i already have open\",\"already-open browser\"]}\naside-devtools-aliases {\"note\":\"Bare aside is kept: without it, requests such as \\\"run aside on the pricing page\\\" or \\\"open aside and log in\\\" name the tool and still defer. Stage two only runs after the advisor picks this hub, so ordinary-prose uses of the word never reach it.\",\"keywords\":[\"aside\",\"aside browser\",\"aside cli\",\"aside mcp\",\"aside repl\",\"aside daemon\",\"aside account\",\"aside devtools\",\"mcp-aside-devtools\"]}\n== attach to my own chrome and finish the checkout\nroute single mcp-chrome-devtools\n== use my signed-in chrome to fill the form in aside\nroute orderedBundle mcp-chrome-devtools,mcp-aside-devtools\n== in my logged in chrome, work out how to finish this signup\nroute single mcp-chrome-devtools\n22:Routing has two stages. `hub-router.json` scores the request and selects one workflow mode, an ordered bundle, or a defer outcome, and `mode-registry.json` maps that mode to its packet folder. This file then picks the leaves inside the selected packet. It never re-decides the mode.\n30:Generic browser-automation phrasing names no tool, so it fires no intent here and the hub defers. That covers \"browser automation\", \"agentic browser\" and \"ai browser automation\": a bare agentic request belongs to neither Aside nor Bladebro.\n45:# a request that fires no intent takes the hub's defer fallback.\n51:    \"CHROME_DEVTOOLS\":  {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"chrome devtools\", \"open devtools\", \"via devtools\", \"use devtools\", \"in devtools\", \"devtools console\", \"browser debug\", \"bdg\", \"cdp\", \"chrome-devtools\", \"mcp-chrome-devtools\", \"inspect the dom\", \"screenshot capture\", \"console errors\", \"network requests\", \"har export\", \"export a har\", \"har file\", \"cdp domain\", \"capture browser screenshots\", \"chrome_devtools_live\", \"chrome devtools live\", \"remote debugging\", \"chrome autoconnect\", \"my own chrome\", \"signed-in chrome\", \"logged in chrome\"]},\n84:- No keyword match is the hub's defer fallback: confirm the browser mode before loading anything.\n105:> Follow the returned decision: `route` uses its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask for disambiguation, and `reject` refuses. On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the registry routing in `hub-router.json`. Set `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=0` to force legacy routing for every hub.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"is