{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Aj8yffoVhjjJQmfVFQVG11","type":"tool_result","content":"specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:3:description: \"Two alignment runs over the browser hub found 112 defects: docs that name commands bdg 0.6.10 rejects, scripts that fail on macOS, Code Mode blocks that never run and a routing m\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:8:  - \"own chrome attach routing lift\"\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:59:The browser hub's docs and scripts describe a bdg and a Code Mode that no longer behave that way. Readers copy `bdg cdp` calls with positional JSON, which bdg 0.6.10 rejects. They also copy C\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:90:- Lift the advisor's read-only floor for an own-Chrome attach request, with a negative control.\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:105:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | Modify | Own-Chrome attach lift |\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:122:| REQ-003 | An own-Chrome attach request routes to the hub | `run-probes.cjs` prints `pass=9 fail=0` for the P03 probe file |\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:151:| Risk | A read-only lift captures unrelated prompts | Med | The lift needs an attach verb, and two negative controls pin it in `route-gates.vitest.ts` |\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/implementation-summary.md:3:description: \"The browser hub's docs and scripts now match bdg 0.6.10 and Code Mode, and an own-Chrome attach request routes to Chrome DevTools. All 112 alignment findings ar\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/implementation-summary.md:52:The browser hub's commands now run as written. A `bdg cdp` call passes its JSON through `--params`, Code Mode blocks drop top-level `await`, `install.sh` finds Chrome on mac\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/implementation-summary.md:70:| `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` and `tests/scorer/route-gates.vitest.ts` | Modified | Own-Chrome attach lift and its tests |\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/implementation-summary.md:95:| The own-Chrome lift needs an attach verb | \"my own Chrome\" or \"logged-in Chrome\" alone also opens questions about browser settings, and a first draft routed \"Explain what \nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/001-research/research/research.md:14:- **Aside overlap (KQ8):** **no.** Bladebro does not take over Aside's deterministic signed-in work. Aside keeps that work, and Bladebro gets the stealth, caller-owned-browser and agentic signed-in cases through t\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/001-research/research/research.md:42:| Signed-in profiles | `rb on` \"your browser\": attach / clone / profile, injection off | `chrome_devtools_live --autoConnect`, fallback only | signed-in account by default, `--account`, autofill |\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/001-research/research/research.md:138:macOS constraint: `profile` mode needs the browser closed, and branded Chrome 136+ refuses remote debugging on its default data directory, so the plan defaults to `clone`/`auto` and keeps `attach` for a browser t\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/001-research/research/research.md:146:| R-SEC-1 signed-in profiles | `rb` acts in authenticated sessions; \"Actions in a signed-in profile can affect your account\" | owned agent-browser profile by default (`BLADE_HOME`/`BLADE_FRESH=1`); `rb` only on e\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/001-research/research/research.md:162:**Cases that go to Bladebro (complement, not takeover):** stealth on a signed-in site, `rb attach` to a caller-owned browser that must stay open, and agentic branching signed-in workflows. The tie-break routes de\n30:| **mcp-bladebro** | Stealth browsing, agentic branching and caller-owned browser attachment through Bladebro | `mcp-bladebro/` |\n45:| Signed-in profile | `chrome_devtools_live --autoConnect` | Signed-in account by default | Attach to, clone or profile the caller's browser |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:47:44.861Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:3:description: \"Two alignment runs over the browser hub found 112 defects: docs that name commands bdg 0.6.10 rejects, scripts that fail on macOS, Code Mode blocks that never run and a routing m\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:8:  - \"own chrome attach routing lift\"\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:59:The browser hub's docs and scripts describe a bdg and a Code Mode that no longer behave that way. Readers copy `bdg cdp` calls with positional JSON, which bdg 0.6.10 rejects. They also copy C\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:90:- Lift the advisor's read-only floor for an own-Chrome attach request, with a negative control.\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:1