specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/goal.md`, `spec.md`","+- `specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/00{2,3,4,5}-*/goal.md`","+- `specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/005-routing-and-surfaces/implementation-summary.md`, `spec.md`, `scratch/after-stage1.jsonl`","+- `specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/tasks.md`","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mode-registry.json`, `.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mode-registry.json`","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md`, `.utcp_config.json`","+- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/mcp-mutation-class-manifest.yaml`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/check-mcp-mutation-class.sh`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/check-mcp-mutation-class.test.sh`, `.skilled/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit`","+- `.skilled/bin/tests/mcp-installers.test.cjs`, `.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/scripts/_utils.sh`, `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh`","+","+## Findings by Severity","+","+### P0 Findings","+","+None.","+","+### P1 Findings","+","+1. **Phase 013 broke phase 003's installer-test criterion: the two `_utils.sh` copies now differ** -- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh:160` -- `node --test .skilled/bin/tests/mcp-installers.test.cjs` now fails its first test, \"both copies of the helper library are identical\" (`.skilled/bin/tests/mcp-installers.test.cjs:49-55`). 013's T008 raised the Node minimum to 20 in the Chrome DevTools copy only (`013-.../tasks.md:50`, commit `1a350b1512b` touches only that copy), while `.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/scripts/_utils.sh:160` still reads `min_version=\"${1:-18}\"` and line 164 still hard-codes \"Node.js 18+\". The test header states the rule outright: \"change both copies together\". Phase 003's goal criterion (`003-mode-relocation/goal.md:61`) requires this test to exit 0, so a shipped, previously passing criterion is now false, and 013's verification (`bash -n` plus one `rg` line) never ran the suite that guards the file it edited.","+   Finding class: regression (cross-phase).","+   Scope proof: `diff` of the two copies prints exactly two hunks, lines 160 and 164; the test run reports the assertion at `mcp-installers.test.cjs:51`.","+   Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/scripts/_utils.sh`, `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh`, `.skilled/bin/tests/mcp-installers.test.cjs`, 013 tasks T008 verify step.","+   Case: run `node --test .skilled/bin/tests/mcp-installers.test.cjs` on the current tree; the identical-copies test fails with the \"change both copies together\" message.","+","+```json","+{\"type\":\"regression\",\"claim\":\"013 changed only the Chrome DevTools _utils.sh copy, so mcp-installers.test.cjs fails and 003 goal criterion 4 no longer holds\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/bin/tests/mcp-installers.test.cjs:49\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/scripts/_utils.sh:160\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh:160\",\"specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/tasks.md:50\",\"specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/003-mode-relocation/goal.md:61\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Checked whether the test was retired or whether the code-mode copy was intentionally left at 18: the test is live and its header requires lockstep changes; no decision record exempts the code-mode copy\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"Code Mode may genuinely support Node 18, but then the test and the shared-library design must change; as shipped, the gate fails\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to P2 if a recorded decision intentionally splits the two helpers and the test is updated to match\"}","+```","+","+### P2 Findings","+","+2. **Phases 003 and 004 are marked Complete but every completion criterion in their goal.md is unchecked** -- `specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/003-mode-relocation/goal.md:58` -- Lines 58-62 of 003's goal and lines 59-63 of 004's goal are all `- [ ]`, while the parent phase map lists both as Complete (`spec.md:118-119`). Re-run here, 003's criteria 1, 2, 3 and 5 and 004's criteria 1-4 hold; 003's criterion 4 is false (finding 1). The goal file is the only source of goal state, so a reader cannot tell done from not-done without re-running everything.","+   Finding class: traceability-drift.","+   Scope proof: `grep -n '^- \\[ \\]'` over both goal files prints ten lines; the parent `spec.md` phase map rows 3 and 4 say Complete.","+   Affected surface hints: `003-mode-relocation/goal.md`, `004-bladebro-mode/goal.md`, parent `spec.md` phase map.","+   Case: an operator reads 003's goal to decide whether the phase is closed; all five boxes are empty although the phase is reported Complete.","+","+3. **005 goal criterion 1 is ticked though its own evidence shows mcp-tooling still passing the threshold** -- `specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/005-routing-and-surfaces/goal.md:59` -- The criterion reads \"returns mcp-browser-use above threshold ... and mcp-tooling for none of them\" and is `[x]`. The phase's evidence file records `\"mcp_tooling_passing\": true` for all three mode requests (`005-.../scratch/after-stage1.jsonl:1-3`), and the summary concedes mcp-tooling is \"Still listed at 0.54 to 0.58\" (`005-.../implementation-summary.md:133`). `005-.../spec.md:23` honestly records REQ-003 as met only at the default threshold; the goal checkbox drops that qualifier.","+   Finding class: traceability-drift.","+   Scope proof: three of three stage-one rows carry `mcp_tooling_passing: true`.","+   Affected surface hints: `005-routing-and-surfaces/goal.md`, parent `goal.md` progress row for 005.","+   Case: replay the first prompt with `--threshold 0.5`; mcp-tooling passes, contradicting the ticked criterion.","+","+## Traceability Checks","+","+| Protocol | Status | Evidence |","+|----------|--------|----------|","+| spec_code | partial | Parent criteria 2-5 hold: registry counts 3 and 6 (`.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mode-registry.json`), stale-path `rg` empty, `parent-skill-check.cjs` OK for both hubs, advisor plus compiled route return `mcp-browser-use` with `action: route`. 003 criterion 4 fails (finding 1). |","+| checklist_evidence | partial | 003/004 goal boxes unchecked (finding 2); 005 criterion 1 ticked against its own evidence (finding 3). |","+","+## Integration Evidence","+","+- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs` on `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use`: \"OK: parent-skill-check — all hard invariants passed, 0 warnings\".","+- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/check-mcp-mutation-class.test.sh`: \"Results: 51 passed, 0 failed\", with an `mcp-browser-use/mcp-other` case at line 145.","+- `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` for a Bladebro attach request: `mcp-browser-use` 0.928 with `compiledRoute.action: route`, `selectionKind: single`.","+- `.utcp_config.json` holds a `bladebro` stdio manual with `args: [\"mcp\"]`.","+","+## Edge Cases","+","+- 003's goal lists `check-mcp-mutation-class.test.sh` at no path; it lives under `scripts/tests/`. Resolved by search, not a finding.","+- 004 criterion 5 (`git diff --stat` on Aside prints nothing) is a point-in-time check that later phases (008, 013) legitimately invalidate; treated as historical, not re-scored.","+","+## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces","+","+- Hub registry: three modes, each `packetKind workflow`, `backendKind cli-plus-mcp`, `advisorRouting.routingClass metadata`, no `extensions` key (002 criteria 2-3).","+- Mutation guard: manifest `skill_dir` lines 45, 61, 68 point under `mcp-browser-use`; pre-commit regex line 726 and `HOOK_PATTERN`/`DISCOVERY_GLOBS` name `mcp-browser-use/`.","+- Bladebro SKILL.md: `name: mcp-bladebro`, `command -v bladebro` lane check, six R-SEC mentions.","+","+## Ruled Out","+","+- Stale `mcp-tooling/mcp-chrome-devtools` or `mcp-tooling/mcp-aside-devtools` paths under `.skilled` outside changelog/benchmark reports: none.","+- Browser mode ids in mcp-tooling's own six root files: none.","+","+## Next Focus","+","+- Dimension: security","+- Focus area: 004 R-SEC rules vs spec section 3 text, Bladebro/Aside install and doctor scripts, `.utcp_config.json` env handling, shell scripts in the hub (`shared/`, `scripts/`).","+- Reason: the hub ships executable install scripts and a stealth/real-browser driver; trust boundaries not yet covered.","+- Rotation status: correctness done; security, traceability, maintainability remain.","+- Required evidence: file:line in scripts and R-SEC text comparison.","+","+Review verdict: CONDITIONAL"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-3/iterations/iteration-001.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012uHrYPUFns8vKgitSkPbqL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
