{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016bKA6VSZpjopLvFbyXUyDq","type":"tool_result","content":".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/doctor.sh:36:  info \"Install (operator-invoked): curl -fsSL <url> | bash\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:2:# WHY: operator-invoked wrapper around the official Aside curl installer.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:31:    3. Runs the official installer: curl -fsSL <url> | bash\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:74:command -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || { err \"curl not found — required to fetch the installer\"; exit 1; }\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:77:info \"curl -fsSL $INSTALLER_URL | bash\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:78:if curl -fsSL \"$INSTALLER_URL\" | bash; then\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:45:    3. Runs: npm install -g bladebro@${PINNED_VERSION}\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:110:info \"npm install -g bladebro@${PINNED_VERSION}\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:111:if ! npm install -g \"bladebro@${PINNED_VERSION}\"; then\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:112:  err \"npm install failed; see the output above\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/install.sh:230:    if npm install -g \"${MCP_PACKAGE}\"; then\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/install.sh:235:        log_info \"Try running: sudo npm install -g ${MCP_PACKAGE}\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh:843:    if eval \"$cmd\" &>/dev/null; then\n---\n- Expected execution process: run the commands in order from the repository root on macOS, read each output and exit status, then judge them against the pass/fail criteria.\n- Expected signals: the doctor prints the data root, the operator confirms no needed named session remains in it, npm exits 0, step 5 prints `absent` and step 6 prints `root absent`\n- Desired user-visible outcome: The host is clean, and no named session the operator still needed was deleted.\n- Pass/fail: PASS if the package and the doctor-reported data root are gone after the operator's confirmation. FAIL if either remains, or if the root was removed without that confirmation.\n\n---\n\n## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n\n### Prompt\n\n- Prompt: `Uninstall Bladebro and remove its data folder.`\n\n### Commands\n\n1. `bladebro doctor`, and record the data root it prints as `<root>`. Run it before the uninstall, because the binary is gone afterwards. The root is `~/.local/state/blade`, a previously used `~/.blade`, or whatever `BLADE_HOME` points to.\n2. `ls -la \"<root>\"`, then ask the operator to confirm that no named session in it is still needed.\n3. `npm uninstall -g bladebro`\n4. `rm -rf \"<root>\"`, with the path from step 1, only after the confirmation in step 2.\n5. `command -v bladebro || echo absent`\n6. `test -e \"<root>\" && echo \"root remains\" || echo \"root absent\"`\n\n### Expected\n\n- Step 1 names the data root.\n- The operator's confirmation from step 2 is recorded.\n- `removed N packages`\n- `absent`\n- `root absent`\n\n### Evidence\n\nAll outputs, the data root step 1 printed, and the operator's confirmation from step 2.\n\n### Pass / Fail\n\n- **Pass**: the package and the doctor-reported data root are gone, and the root was removed only after the operator's confirmation.\n- **Fail**: either remains, or the root was removed without the confirmation.\n\n### Failure Triage\n\n1. Without operator approval, do not run this scenario. Record `SKIP` with the missing approval as the blocker.\n2. If the operator still needs a named session, stop after step 3, keep the data root, and record `SKIP` for the root removal with that reason.\n3. If step 6 prints `root remains`, compare the path against the one step 1 printed before running anything else.\n\n---\n\n## 4. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Playbook Sources","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:49:07.735Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/doctor.sh:36:  info \"Install (operator-invoked): curl -fsSL <url> | bash\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:2:# WHY: operator-invoked wrapper around the official Aside curl installer.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:31:    3. Runs the official installer: curl -fsSL <url> | bash\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:74:command -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || { err \"curl not found — required to fetch the installer\"; exit 1; }\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:77:info \"curl -fsSL $INSTALLER_URL | bash\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:78:if curl -fsSL \"$INSTALLER_URL\" | bash; then\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:45:    3. Runs: npm install -g bladebro@${PINNED_VERSION}\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:110:info \"npm install -g bladebro@${PINNED_VERSION}\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:111:if ! npm install -g \"bladebro@${PINNED_VERSION}\"; then\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:112:  err \"npm install failed; see the output above\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/install.sh:230:    if npm install -g \"${MCP_PACKAGE}\"; then\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/install.sh:235:        log_info \"Try running: sudo npm install -g ${MCP_PACKAGE}\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh:843:    if eval \"$cmd\" &>