{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM9eamNDZmcyN2bjYkxm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01698F9tXLZYdxdMycQa43PX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-2; cat > $L/iterations/iteration-002.md <<'EOF'\n# Iteration 002 — Security: install supply chain, signed-in profile rules, teardown\n\n## Dispatcher\n- Lineage opus-2, iteration 2 (state log held 1 iteration row). steer.md absent.\n\n## Dimension\nsecurity\n\n## Review Focus Coverage\nChecked phase 004's R-SEC-1/2/3 goal criteria and phase 007's install-script parity against the shipped scripts, the prior generation's teardown fix (R2-P1-001), and the UTCP manuals phase 004 added for the Code Mode fallback.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:1-150`\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:112-116` (R-SEC-1/2/3)\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:30-75`\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:20-80`, `doctor.sh:36`\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh:837-850`, `install.sh:230`\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md:83,89,142`\n- `.utcp_config.json` (aside, bladebro, chrome_devtools_1/2/live manuals)\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n1. **Bladebro installer runs npm lifecycle scripts before the digest gate it exists to enforce** -- .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:111 -- `npm install -g \"bladebro@${PINNED_VERSION}\"` runs without `--ignore-scripts`, so any install or postinstall hook in the package executes before the SHA-256 check at lines 130-138. The header (lines 5-9, 18-20) says an unverifiable binary \"is the thing this wrapper exists to prevent\", and R-SEC-3 (SKILL.md:116) says to verify the resolved native package \"before use\". The check also covers only the native binary; the JS launcher at `$(npm prefix -g)/bin/bladebro`, which is what runs at line 142 and on PATH, is never compared against anything. Reach is a tampered or substituted 4.8.2 tarball on the operator's configured registry; npm version immutability and the operator stop-for-yes keep this at hardening level.\n   Finding class: supply-chain hardening gap against a stated security rule.\n   Scope proof: install.sh:111 vs install.sh:130-138 ordering; SKILL.md:116.\n   Affected surface hints: mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh, INSTALL-GUIDE.md install steps, R-SEC-3 wording.\n   Case: a registry-served bladebro@4.8.2 whose package.json declares a postinstall hook runs that hook during install.sh line 111 even when the later digest check fails and uninstalls the package.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n- spec_code (pass for security surfaces): R-SEC-1 \"never pass --account to aside mcp or aside repl\" is reflected in Aside SKILL.md:89 and :142 and the examples README; the teardown playbook now reads the root from `bladebro doctor`, waits for operator confirmation and asserts `root absent` (uninstall-and-data-root.md:47-52), so the prior R2-P1-001 fix holds.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n- `.utcp_config.json` manuals carry `env: {}` for aside, bladebro and the three chrome_devtools servers; no secret values. chrome-devtools-mcp is pinned at 0.26.0.\n\n## Edge Cases\n- Aside's install.sh pipes the vendor installer (`curl -fsSL <url> | bash`, line 78) with no pin or digest and honors `ASIDE_CLI_BASE_URL` from the environment. It is operator-invoked and the vendor's documented path; no goal or R-SEC rule covers Aside's install, so it is recorded here rather than as a finding.\n- `verify_command` in chrome-devtools `_utils.sh:837` uses `eval \"$cmd\"` but has no caller in the scripts folder; unreachable today.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n- Bladebro install refuses non-macOS and unknown arch, never replaces an existing install, never runs `npm update`/`bladebro -u`, and uninstalls on digest mismatch.\n- R-SEC-2: `blocked:` is terminal in SKILL.md:114.\n\n## Ruled Out\n- Unconditional `rm -rf` of the Bladebro data root: fixed (playbook steps 1-6).\n- Secrets in UTCP browser manuals: none.\n\n## Next Focus\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: each phase's goal.md completion criteria against implementation-summary.md evidence and the parent spec status table; spec_code and checklist_evidence core protocols.\n- Reason: operator focus is phase goals vs shipped work; parent spec.md shows Status Complete while the phase map marks 005 Partial and the 006→007 handoff row is TBD.\n- Required evidence: goal.md criteria lines and the evidence each implementation-summary cites.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\nEOF\ncat > /tmp/opus2dr/s2.json <<'EOF'\n{\"iteration\":2,\"focus\":\"security: install supply chain, R-SEC rules, teardown\",\"dimensions\":[\"security\"],\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-24T04:52:00Z\",\n\"filesReviewed\":[\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:111\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:116\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:47\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:78\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh:837\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md:89\",\".utcp_config.json\"],\n\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"O2-I2-P2-001\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"dimension\":\"security\",\"title\":\"Bladebro installer runs npm lifecycle scripts before the digest gate, and the JS launcher is never verified\",\"file\":\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:111\",\"findingClass\":\"supply-chain-hardening\",\"scopeProof\":\"install.sh:111 precedes digest check at 130-138; SKILL.md:116 R-SEC-3\",\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh\",\"mcp-bladebro/INSTALL-GUIDE.md\"]}],\n\"traceability\":[{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md:89\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:47\"],\"summary\":\"R-SEC rules reflected in Aside and Bladebro surfaces; teardown fix holds\"}],\n\"ruledOut\":[{\"direction\":\"unconditional rm -rf of Bladebro data root\",\"reason\":\"playbook now reads root from bladebro doctor and requires operator confirmation\"},{\"direction\":\"secrets in UTCP browser manuals\",\"reason\":\"env {} for all five manuals\"}],\n\"ratio\":0.5,\"justification\":\"one new P2 (weight 1) against 2 accumulated weighted findings\"}\nEOF\nnode /tmp/opus2dr/rec.js /tmp/opus2dr/s2.json 2>&1 | cut -c1-160","description":"Write iteration 2 artifacts and reduce"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2550,"cache_read_input_tokens":166333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2550},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:50:04.321Z","request_id":"<redacted>","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01698F9tXLZYdxdMycQa43PX":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-2; cat > $L/iterations/iteration-002.md <<'EOF'\n# Iteration 002 — Security: install supply chain, signed-in profile rules, teardown\n\n## Dispatcher\n- Lineage opus-2, iteration 2 (state log held 1 iteration row). steer.md absent.\n\n## Dimension\nsecurity\n\n## Review Focus Coverage\nChecked phase 004's R-SEC-1/2/3 goal criteria and phase 007's install-script parity against the shipped scripts, the prior generation's teardown fix (R2-P1-001), and the UTCP manuals phase 004 added for the Code Mode fallback.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:1-150`\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:112-116` (R-SEC-1/2/3)\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:30-75`\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:20-80`, `doctor.sh:36`\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh:837-850`, `install.sh:230`\n- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md:83,89,142`\n- `.utcp_config.json` (aside, bladebro, chrome_devtools_1/2/live manuals)\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n1. **Bladebro installer runs npm lifecycle scripts before the digest gate it exists to enforce** -- .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:111 -- `npm install -g \"bladebro@${PINNED_VERSION}\"` runs without `--ignore-scripts`, so any install or postinstall hook in the package executes before the SHA-256 check at lines 130-138. The header (lines 5-9, 18-20) says an unverifiable binary \"is the thing this wrapper exists to prevent\", and R-SEC-3 (SKILL.md:116) says to verify the resolved native package \"before use\". The check also covers only the native binary; the JS launcher at `$(npm prefix -g)/bin/bladebro`, which is what runs at line 142 and on PATH, is never compared against anything. Reach is a tampered or substituted 4.8.2 tarball on the operator's configured registry; npm version immutability and the operator stop-for-yes keep this at hardening level.\n   Finding class: supply-chain hardening gap against a stated security rule.\n   Scope proof: install.sh:111 vs install.sh:130-138 ordering; SKILL.md:116.\n   Affected surface hints: mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh, INSTALL-GUIDE.md install steps, R-SEC-3 wording.\n   Case: a registry-served bladebro@4.8.2 whose package.json declares a postinstall hook runs that hook during install.sh line 111 even when the later digest check fails and uninstalls the package.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n- spec_code (pass for security surfaces): R-SEC-1 \"never pass --account to aside mcp or aside repl\" is reflected in Aside SKILL.md:89 and :142 and the examples README; the teardown playbook now reads the root from `bladebro doctor`, waits for operator confirmation and asserts `root absent` (uninstall-and-data-root.md:47-52), so the prior R2-P1-001 fix holds.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n- `.utcp_config.json` manuals carry `env: {}` for aside, bladebro and the three chrome_devtools servers; no secret values. chrome-devtools-mcp is pinned at 0.26.0.\n\n## Edge Cases\n- Aside's install.sh pipes the vendor installer (`curl -fsSL <url> | bash`, line 78) with no pin or digest and honors `ASIDE_CLI_BASE_URL` from the environment. It is operator-invoked and the vendor's documented path; no goal or R-SEC rule covers Aside's install, so it is recorded here rather than as a finding.\n- `verify_command` in chrome-devtools `_utils.sh:837` uses `eval \"$cmd\"` but has no caller in the scripts folder; unreachable today.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n- Bladebro install refuses non-macOS and unknown arch, never replaces an existing install, never runs `npm update`/`bladebro -u`, and uninstalls on digest mismatch.\n- R-SEC-2: `blocked:` is terminal in SKILL.md:114.\n\n## Ruled Out\n- Unconditional `rm -rf` of the Bladebro data root: fixed (playbook steps 1-6).\n- Secrets in UTCP browser manuals: none.\n\n## Next Focus\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: each phase's goal.md completion criteria against implementation-summary.md evidence and the parent spec status table; spec_code and checklist_evidence core protocols.\n- Reason: operator focus is phase goals vs shipped work; parent spec.md shows Status Complete while the phase map marks 005 Partial and the 006→007 handoff row is TBD.\n- Required evidence: goal.md criteria lines and the evidence each implementation-summary cites.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\nEOF\ncat > /tmp/opus2dr/s2.json <<'EOF'\n{\"iteration\":2,\"focus\":\"security: install supply chain, R-SEC rules, teardown\",\"dimensions\":[\"security\"],\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-24T04:52:00Z\",\n\"filesReviewed\":[\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:111\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:116\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:47\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:78\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh:837\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md:89\",\".utcp_config.json\"],\n\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"O2-I2-P2-001\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"dimension\":\"security\",\"title\":\"Bladebro installer runs npm lifecycle scripts before the digest gate, and the JS launcher is never verified\",\"file\":\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:111\",\"findingClass\":\"supply-chain-hardening\",\"scopeProof\":\"install.sh:111 precedes digest check at 130-138; SKILL.md:116 R-SEC-3\",\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh\",\"mcp-bladebro/INSTALL-GUIDE.md\"]}],\n\"traceability\":[{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md:89\",\".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:47\"],\"summary\":\"R-SEC rules reflected in Aside and Bladebro surfaces; teardown fix holds\"}],\n\"ruledOut\":[{\"direction\":\"unconditional rm -rf of Bladebro data root\",\"reason\":\"playbook now reads root from bladebro doctor and requires operator confirmation\"},{\"direction\":\"secrets in UTCP browser manuals\",\"reason\":\"env {} for all five manuals\"}],\n\"ratio\":0.5,\"justification\":\"one new P2 (weight 1) against 2 accumulated weighted findings\"}\nEOF\nnode /tmp/opus2dr/rec.js /tmp/opus2dr/s2.json 2>&1 | cut -c1-160","description":"Write iteration 2 artifacts and reduce"}}}
