{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V9E2ydKxwhYpDxZJm8fbbz","type":"tool_result","content":"9:> **EXECUTION POLICY**: Every scenario MUST be executed for real — not mocked, not stubbed, not classified as \"unautomatable\". AI agents executing these scenarios must run the actual commands, inspect real files, call real handlers, and verify real outputs. The only acceptable classifications are PASS, FAIL, or SKIP (with a specific sandbox blocker documented). \"UNAUTOMATABLE\" is not a valid status.\n11:This document combines the full manual-validation contract for the `mcp-aside-devtools` skill into a single reference. The root playbook acts as the operator directory, review protocol, and orchestration guide while per-feature files carry the scenario-specific execution truth. Aside is the AI-browser surface for OpenCode; the CLI (`aside`) is the primary interface with two lanes (agent tasks and the deterministic REPL), while the Aside MCP server (`aside mcp`, stdio) is the Code Mode composition fallback — its `aside` UTCP manual is registered in `.utcp_config.json`, and the Code Mode discovery scenario needs a session with the code_mode MCP loaded.\n29:A scenario run is complete only after its `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `SKIP` outcome and reason are recorded into `mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`.\n35:This playbook provides 29 deterministic scenarios across 8 categories (7 operator categories plus the routing-recall contracts) validating the `mcp-aside-devtools` skill surface. Each scenario maps to a dedicated feature file with the canonical objective, prompt summary, expected signals, and feature-file reference.\n42:4. The scenario passes only when the workflow is sound and the returned artifact (screenshot file, fixture, discovered inventory) is independently verified.\n46:- The MCP tool inventory is version-pinned evidence (one `repl` tool on `1.26.626.1517`) — scenarios assert *discovery ran*, not that the inventory matches forever.\n47:- Console capture (ASD-012) and network capture (ASD-013) began as guarded probes with no verified contract. ASD-018 then documented the Playwright `page.on(...)` pattern, but on Aside 1.26.626.1517 `page.on('console')`, `page.on('request')` and `page.on('response')` each throw an error that lists the supported page events and points to `page.console.logs()`, and `page.context()` does not exist. The probes and ASD-018 record that per-event outcome; live execution still needs a bound authorized session, so ASD-016..021 are SKIP-valid without one.\n48:- The DevTools-parity family (ASD-016..021) mirrors the Chrome DevTools capability surface through the fixture-confirmed Playwright `page` API. Two honest gaps stay flagged, never claimed: **no native HAR export** (assemble a HAR-equivalent from events) and **no Lighthouse audit** (Performance-API timing only).\n      22\nprobes-and-gaps/console-probe.md\nprobes-and-gaps/network-probe.md\ndevtools-parity/performance-timing.md\ndevtools-parity/screenshot-pdf-capture.md\ndevtools-parity/cookies-storage.md\ndevtools-parity/navigation-multi-tab.md\ndevtools-parity/dom-query-inspection.md\ndevtools-parity/console-network-capture.md\nagent-task/direct-task.md\nagent-task/session-continuation.md\ncli-lifecycle/account-status.md\ncli-lifecycle/help-fixture.md\ncli-lifecycle/install-version.md\nrecovery-and-failure/missing-binary.md\nrecovery-and-failure/dead-mcp-process.md\nmcp-transport/code-mode-discovery.md\nmcp-transport/unbound-profile-error.md\nmcp-transport/tools-list-discovery.md\nmcp-transport/mcp-handshake.md\nintra-routing-recall/troubleshoot.md\nintra-routing-recall/mcp.md\nintra-routing-recall/holdout-troubleshoot.md\nintra-routing-recall/install.md\nintra-routing-recall/task.md\nintra-routing-recall/repl.md\nintra-routing-recall/holdout-repl.md\nintra-routing-recall/negative.md\nrepl-evidence/repl-open-tab.md\nrepl-evidence/repl-screenshot-artifact.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:52:42.323Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"9:> **EXECUTION POLICY**: Every scenario MUST be executed for real — not mocked, not stubbed, not classified as \"unautomatable\". AI agents executing these scenarios must run the actual commands, inspect real files, call real handlers, and verify real outputs. The only acceptable classifications are PASS, FAIL, or SKIP (with a specific sandbox blocker documented). \"UNAUTOMATABLE\" is not a valid status.\n11:This document combines the full manual-validation contract for the `mcp-aside-devtools` skill into a single reference. The root playbook acts as the operator directory, review protocol, and orchestration guide while per-feature files carry the scenario-specific execution truth. Aside is the AI-browser surface for OpenCode; the CLI (`aside`) is the primary interface with two lanes (agent tasks and the deterministic REPL), while the Aside MCP server (`aside mcp`, stdio) is the Code Mode composition fallback — its `aside` UTCP manual is registered in `.utcp_config.json`, and the Code Mode discovery scenario needs a session with the code_mode MCP loaded.\n29:A scenario run is complete only after its `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `SKIP` outcome and reason are recorded into `mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`.\n35:This playbook provides 29 deterministic scenarios across 8 categories (7 operator categories plus the routing-recall contracts) validating the `mcp-aside-devtools` skill surface. Each scenario maps to a dedicated feature file with the canonical objective, prompt summary, expected signals, and feature-file reference.\n42:4. The scenario passes only when the workflow is sound and the returned artifact (screenshot file, fixture, discovered inventory) is independently verified.\n46:- The MCP tool inventory is version-pinned evidence (one `repl` tool on `1.26.626.1517`) — scenarios assert *discovery ran*, not that the inventory matches forever.\n47:- Console capture (ASD-012) and network capture (ASD-013) began as guarded probes with no verified contract. ASD-018 then documented the Playwright `page.on(...)` pattern, but on Aside 1.26.626.1517 `page.on('console')`, `page.on('request')` and `page.on('response')` each throw an error that lists the supported page events and points to `page.console.logs()`, and `page.context()` does not exist. The probes and ASD-018 record that per-event outcome; live execution still needs a bound authorized session, so ASD-016..021 are SKIP-valid without one.\n48:- The DevTools-parity family (ASD-016..021) mirrors the Chrome DevTools capability surface through the fixture-confirmed Playwright `page` API. Two honest gaps stay flagged, never claimed: **no native HAR export** (assemble a HAR-equivalent from events) and **no Lighthouse audit** (Performance-API timing only).\n      22\nprobes-and-gaps/console-probe.md\nprobes-and-gaps/network-probe.md\ndevtools-parity/performance-timing.md\ndevtools-parity/screenshot-pdf-capture.md\ndevtools-parity/cookies-storage.md\ndevtools-parity/navigation-multi-tab.md\ndevtools-parity/dom-query-inspection.md\ndevtools-parity/console-network-capture.md\nagent-task/direct-task.md\nagent-task/session-continuation.md\ncli-lifecycle/account-status.md\ncli-lifecycle/help-fixture.md\ncli-lifecycle/install-version.md\nrecovery-and-failure/missing-binary.md\nrecovery-and-failure/dead-mcp-process.md\nmcp-transport/code-mode-discovery.md\nmcp-transport/unbound-profile-error.md\nmcp-transport/tools-list-discovery.md\nmcp-transport/mcp-handshake.md\nintra-routing-recall/troubleshoot.md\nintra-routing-recall/mcp.md\nintra-routing-recall/holdout-troubleshoot.md\nintra-routing-recall/install.md\nintra-routing-recall/task.md\nintra-routing-recall/repl.md\nintra-routing-recall/holdout-repl.md\nintra-routing-recall/negative.md\nrepl-evidence/repl-open-tab.md\nrepl-evidence/repl-screenshot-artifact.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":f