{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0151N4xr5XsVjCSep567qJeP","type":"tool_result","content":"7. Claim a *native dedicated* console/network tool, a *native HAR export*, a *Lighthouse audit*, *parallel isolated instances* or *raw CDP passthrough*. Aside has none of these.\n\nConsole/network capture IS reachable through Playwright `page.on(...)` events in the repl (fixture-confirmed API). The caller assembles it, so it is not a dedicated tool.\nDocument the pattern and its gaps. Treat any live capture as requiring a bound session and independent verification. See the DevTools-parity feature family.\n### Does Aside capture console logs or network traffic?\n\nYou can collect them yourself through the Playwright `page` API in the REPL. Register `page.on('console', ...)` or `page.on('request', ...)` and keep the events you need. There is no dedicated capture tool and no native HAR export. A live capture needs a bound authorized session, so treat the pattern as unconfirmed until it runs against one.\n\n### Can I run parallel Aside sessions?\nChrome DevTools' Console list and Network panel map onto Playwright event listeners in the repl. Earlier research flagged console/network capture as UNKNOWN because Aside exposes no dedicated `console`/`network` tool. The discovery fixture ([`../../references/discovery-fixture-2026-07-16.json`](../../references/discovery-fixture-2026-07-16.json)) suggested Playwright event listeners: `page.on('con\n\n**Live result on Aside 1.26.626.1517 (2026-11-22, ASD-012, ASD-013 and ASD-018).** `page.on` accepts only close, crash, dialog, domcontentloaded, download, filechooser, frameattached, framedetached, framenavigated, load and popup. It throws for `console`, `request`, `response` and `requestfinished`, so neither capture works through these listeners on this version. The error points to `page.console\n\nCapability class: READ-ONLY (listeners observe; they do not mutate). Honest gap: there is **no native HAR export** (contrast `bdg network har`). You collect `request`/`response` events and assemble a HAR-equivalent yourself; call it \"Playwright-assembled HAR-equivalent\", never a HAR export.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:52:55.610Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"7. Claim a *native dedicated* console/network tool, a *native HAR export*, a *Lighthouse audit*, *parallel isolated instances* or *raw CDP passthrough*. Aside has none of these.\n\nConsole/network capture IS reachable through Playwright `page.on(...)` events in the repl (fixture-confirmed API). The caller assembles it, so it is not a dedicated tool.\nDocument the pattern and its gaps. Treat any live capture as requiring a bound session and independent verification. See the DevTools-parity feature family.\n### Does Aside capture console logs or network traffic?\n\nYou can collect them yourself through the Playwright `page` API in the REPL. Register `page.on('console', ...)` or `page.on('request', ...)` and keep the events you need. There is no dedicated capture tool and no native HAR export. A live capture needs a bound authorized session, so treat the pattern as unconfirmed until it runs against one.\n\n### Can I run parallel Aside sessions?\nChrome DevTools' Console list and Network panel map onto Playwright event listeners in the repl. Earlier research flagged console/network capture as UNKNOWN because Aside exposes no dedicated `console`/`network` tool. The discovery fixture ([`../../references/discovery-fixture-2026-07-16.json`](../../references/discovery-fixture-2026-07-16.json)) suggested Playwright event listeners: `page.on('con\n\n**Live result on Aside 1.26.626.1517 (2026-11-22, ASD-012, ASD-013 and ASD-018).** `page.on` accepts only close, crash, dialog, domcontentloaded, download, filechooser, frameattached, framedetached, framenavigated, load and popup. It throws for `console`, `request`, `response` and `requestfinished`, so neither capture works through these listeners on this version. The error points to `page.console\n\nCapability class: READ-ONLY (listeners observe; they do not mutate). Honest gap: there is **no native HAR export** (contrast `bdg network har`). You collect `request`/`response` events and assemble a HAR-equivalent yourself; call it \"Playwright-assembled HAR-equivalent\", never a HAR export.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0151N4xr5XsVjCSep567qJeP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
