{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AxbPvhHfN8DSgbWveNZnZK","type":"tool_result","content":"      step_check_convergence:\n        action: \"Branch on the stop decision that convergence.cjs computed in step_graph_convergence\"\n        algorithm: |\n          The whole stop decision is computed by convergence.cjs from the review config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. This step performs no arithmetic and never recomputes or overrides the result.\n          The ratio signals leave out every iteration that is not evidence-bearing (thought, error, timeout), and stuck_count is loop_counters_json.stuckCount.\n          The script applies this fixed order, first match wins:\n          1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap is evaluated before every veto, the claim-adjudication veto included; failed legal-stop gates are recorded in stop_decision.blockedBy as synthesis evidence.\n          1a. After 3 consecutive failed iterations (status error or timeout), halt the loop and enter synthesis with stop reason error and partial findings.\n          2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n          3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n          3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: the vote is telemetry only and the decision is CONTINUE.\n          4. a STOP candidate exists when every dimension is clean (all_dimensions_clean) or the weighted vote passes (composite_converged). The vote cutoffs follow the configured convergenceThreshold. When neither forms and depth_mode == \"expansive\", a run whose frontier holds at least one answered\n          4a. if iteration_count < min_iterations: CONTINUE (minIterationsNotReached). min_iterations is config.minIterations, else antiConvergence.minIterations, capped at max_iterations; like research, the floor runs on a candidate before the legal-stop gates.\n          4b. if depth_mode == \"expansive\" and the frontier still holds an open or active node: CONTINUE (frontierOpen). It vetoes every review candidate, all_dimensions_clean included, and never creates a stop.\n          5. the nine legal-stop gates run on a candidate: convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, p0ResolutionGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate. Any failed gate gives BLOCKED (blockedStop)\n          6. the graph decision settles the candidate: STOP_ALLOWED keeps STOP, STOP_BLOCKED gives BLOCKED, CONTINUE or a missing graph decision gives CONTINUE.\n          7. a BLOCKED from step 5 or 6 whose blockedBy set matches the blocked_stop rows of the runs before it, with no new finding since, becomes STOP (blockedStop, reasonDetail blockedStreakReached) once that streak, this pass included, reaches config.stuckThreshold. A different blocker set start\n          Bind the outputs from stop_decision, where G is stop_decision.gates and I is stop_decision.inputs.review:\n            decision = stop_decision.decision\n            stopReason = stop_decision.stopReason\n            reason = stop_decision.stopReason when it is not null, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            reason_detail = stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            weighted_stop_score = stop_decision.weightedStopScore\n            stop_blocked = (stop_decision.decision == \"BLOCKED\")\n            blocked_by_json = stop_decision.blockedBy\n            blocked_by_csv = the members of stop_decision.blockedBy joined with commas\n            convergence_gate_pass = G.convergenceGate.pass\n            convergence_gate_score = G.convergenceGate.score","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:53:31.956Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"      step_check_convergence:\n        action: \"Branch on the stop decision that convergence.cjs computed in step_graph_convergence\"\n        algorithm: |\n          The whole stop decision is computed by convergence.cjs from the review config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. This step performs no arithmetic and never recomputes or overrides the result.\n          The ratio signals leave out every iteration that is not evidence-bearing (thought, error, timeout), and stuck_count is loop_counters_json.stuckCount.\n          The script applies this fixed order, first match wins:\n          1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap is evaluated before every veto, the claim-adjudication veto included; failed legal-stop gates are recorded in stop_decision.blockedBy as synthesis evidence.\n          1a. After 3 consecutive failed iterations (status error or timeout), halt the loop and enter synthesis with stop reason error and partial findings.\n          2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n          3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n          3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: the vote is telemetry only and the decision is CONTINUE.\n          4. a STOP candidate exists when every dimension is clean (all_dimensions_clean) or the weighted vote passes (composite_converged). The vote cutoffs follow the configured convergenceThreshold. When neither forms and depth_mode == \"expansive\", a run whose frontier holds at least one answered\n          4a. if iteration_count < min_iterations: CONTINUE (minIterationsNotReached). min_iterations is config.minIterations, else antiConvergence.minIterations, capped at max_iterations; like research, the floor runs on a candidate before the legal-stop gates.\n          4b. if depth_mode == \"expansive\" and the frontier still holds an open or active node: CONTINUE (frontierOpen). It vetoes every review candidate, all_dimensions_clean included, and never creates a stop.\n          5. the nine legal-stop gates run on a candidate: convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, p0ResolutionGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate. Any failed gate gives BLOCKED (blockedStop)\n          6. the graph decision settles the candidate: STOP_ALLOWED keeps STOP, STOP_BLOCKED gives BLOCKED, CONTINUE or a missing graph decision gives CONTINUE.\n          7. a BLOCKED from step 5 or 6 whose blockedBy set matches the blocked_stop rows of the runs before it, with no new finding since, becomes STOP (blockedStop, reasonDetail blockedStreakReached) once that streak, this pass included, reaches config.stuckThreshold. A different blocker set start\n          Bind the outputs from stop_decision, where G is stop_decision.gates and I is stop_decision.inputs.review:\n            decision = stop_decision.decision\n            stopReason = stop_decision.stopReason\n            reason = stop_decision.stopReason when it is not null, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            reason_detail = stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            weighted_stop_score = stop_decision.weightedStopScore\n            stop_blocked = (stop_decision.decision == \"BLOCKED\")\n            blocked_by_json = stop_decision.blockedBy\n            blocked_by_csv = the members of stop_decision.blockedBy joined with commas\n            convergence_gate_pass = G.convergenceGate.pass\n            convergence_gate_score = G.convergenceGate.score","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AxbPvhHfN8DSgbWveNZnZK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
