{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PBqSgEeLcX9wygWmv7xP8K","type":"tool_result","content":"== real-browser/attach-mode-reads.md\n2:title: \"BB-015 -- Reads in the real-browser lane by attaching to a running browser\"\n3:description: \"This scenario validates page reads and an eval for `BB-015` by attaching to a browser the operator already runs on a fixed debug port. It focuses on reaching a signed-in site without copying the profile.\"\n7:# BB-015 -- Reads in the real-browser lane by attaching to a running browser\n15:The attach mechanism of the real-browser lane. BB-011 and BB-012 import a copy of the profile into a second browser. This scenario instead drives the browser the operator already runs, so the live cookies and sessions of that b\n19:On macOS a second instance of a Chromium-family browser launched from a copied profile can expose no page target, which fails BB-012. Attach mode is the other route to a signed-in site, and it needs its own proof.\n25:Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `BB-015` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n27:- Objective: Attach to the running browser, read the confirmed target site, read its model and evaluate the page title, all read-only.\n28:- Real user request: `Attach Bladebro to my running browser and read the site I confirmed, without clicking or typing anything.`\n29:- Prompt: `Attach Bladebro to my running browser and read the site I confirmed, without clicking or typing anything.`\n30:- Expected execution process: the operator confirms the browser, the target site and a browser restart. Run the commands in order from the repository root on macOS, read each output and exit status, then judge them against the \n32:- Desired user-visible outcome: Bladebro reads the signed-in site through the operator's own browser.\n41:- Prompt: `Attach Bladebro to my running browser and read the site I confirmed, without clicking or typing anything.`\n49:5. `bladebro act eval \"'host-match ' + (location.hostname === new URL('<target URL>').hostname) + ' sign-in ' + /sign ?in|log ?in/i.test(document.title)\" --port 9333 --json`\n50:6. Quit the browser, confirm `curl -s <url> gets no answer, then start the browser normally.\n== real-browser/lane-on-clone.md\n19:Clone mode imports the profile and never writes to the source, which is why it is the approved mechanism.\n25:Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `BB-011` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n27:- Objective: Turn the lane on and confirm the import.\n76:| `real-browser/lane-on-clone.md` | Canonical per-feature execution contract |\n== real-browser/real-mode-reads.md\n3:description: \"This scenario validates page reads and an eval in the real-browser lane for `BB-012`. It focuses on see content, see model and act eval working without the injection layer.\"\n25:Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `BB-012` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n47:3. `bladebro act eval \"document.title\" --json`\n67:2. Try another Chromium-family binary only in a new, separately approved run.\n78:| `real-browser/real-mode-reads.md` | Canonical per-feature execution contract |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/../SKILL.md:75:The owned agent-browser profile is the default lane. It needs no request and touches no personal profile. Use `BLADE_HOME` or `BLADE_FRESH=1` to isolate a task.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/../SKILL.md:112:**R-SEC-1 signed-in profiles.** \"Default to the Bladebro-owned agent-browser profile; use `BLADE_HOME`/`BLADE_FRESH=1` for task isolation. Any real-browser (`rb`) lane requires an explicit operator request, and the operator must select the profile/account before control is handed over. Use `attach` whenever the browser must remain caller-owned and open; do not use `profile` on a live branded Chrome. Gate mutations behind `rb pause`/`rb resume` and keep consent-sensitive actions human-in-the-loop. Never pass `--account` to `aside mcp` or `aside repl`, and keep a single-writer lock per account/profile. Re-capture detection output each session and redact cookie/credential values.\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/../mcp-servers/bladebro-mcp/README.md:35:The registered manual is a stdio server that runs `bladebro mcp` with an empty `env`, because the server needs no credential. `BLADE_HOME` or `BLADE_FRESH` go in that `env` only for a task that needs an isolated data root, as a reviewed configuration change. Launching through `npx -y bladebro mcp` instead pulls the package at launch, which counts as an install and needs an operator yes.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/../mcp-servers/bladebro-mcp/README.md:57:Each MCP server process owns one Bladebro data root. Parallel isolated sessions need one process per `BLADE_HOME` or `BLADE_FRESH=1`. A second manual for that purpose is a configuration change the operator approves, and none is registered.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:55:24.850Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"== real-browser/attach-mode-reads.md\n2:title: \"BB-015 -- Reads in the real-browser lane by attaching to a running browser\"\n3:description: \"This scenario validates page reads and an eval for `BB-015` by attaching to a browser the operator already runs on a fixed debug port. It focuses on reaching a signed-in site without copying the profile.\"\n7:# BB-015 -- Reads in the real-browser lane by attaching to a running browser\n15:The attach mechanism of the real-browser lane. BB-011 and BB-012 import a copy of the profile into a second browser. This scenario instead drives the browser the operator already runs, so the live cookies and sessions of that b\n19:On macOS a second instance of a Chromium-family browser launched from a copied profile can expose no page target, which fails BB-012. Attach mode is the other route to a signed-in site, and it needs its own proof.\n25:Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `BB-015` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n27:- Objective: Attach to the running browser, read the confirmed target site, read its model and evaluate the page title, all read-only.\n28:- Real user request: `Attach Bladebro to my running browser and read the site I confirmed, without clicking or typing anything.`\n29:- Prompt: `Attach Bladebro to my running browser and read the site I confirmed, without clicking or typing anything.`\n30:- Expected execution process: the operator confirms the browser, the target site and a browser restart. Run the commands in order from the repository root on macOS, read each output and exit status, then judge them against the \n32:- Desired user-visible outcome: Bladebro reads the signed-in site through the operator's own browser.\n41:- Prompt: `Attach Bladebro to my running browser and read the site I confirmed, without clicking or typing anything.`\n49:5. `bladebro act eval \"'host-match ' + (location.hostname === new URL('<target URL>').hostname) + ' sign-in ' + /sign ?in|log ?in/i.test(document.title)\" --port 9333 --json`\n50:6. Quit the browser, confirm `curl -s <url> gets no answer, then start the browser normally.\n== real-browser/lane-on-clone.md\n19:Clone mode imports the profile and never writes to the source, which is why it is the approved mechanism.\n25:Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `BB-011` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n27:- Objective: Turn the lane on and confirm the import.\n76:| `real-browser/lane-on-clone.md` | Canonical per-feature execution contract |\n== real-browser/real-mode-reads.md\n3:description: \"This scenario validates page reads and an eval in the real-browser lane for `BB-012`. It focuses on see content, see model and act eval working without the injection layer.\"\n25:Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `BB-012` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n47:3. `bladebro act eval \"document.title\" --json`\n67:2. Try another Chromium-family binary only in a new, separately approved run.\n78:| `real-browser/real-mode-reads.md` | Canonical per-feature execution contract |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/../SKILL.md:75:The owned agent-browser profile is the default lane. It needs no request and touches no personal profile. Use `BLADE_HOME` or `BLADE_FRESH=1` to isolate a task.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/../SKILL.md:112:**R-SEC-1 signed-in profiles.** \"Default to the Bladebro-owned agent-browser profile; use `BLADE_HOME`/`BLADE_FRESH=1` for task isolation. Any real-browser (`rb`) lane requires an explicit operator request, and the operator must select the profile/account before control is handed over. Use `attach` whenever the browser must remain caller-owned and open; do not use `profile` on a live branded Chrome. Gate mutations behind `rb pause`/`rb resume` and keep consent-sensitive actions human-in-the-loop. Never pass `--account` to `aside mcp` or `aside repl`, and keep a single-writer lock per account/profile. Re-capture detection output each session and redact cookie/credential values.\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/../mcp-servers/bladebro-mcp/README.md:35:The registered manual is a stdio server that runs `bladebro mcp` with an empty `env`, because the server needs no credential. `BLADE_HOME` or `BLADE_FRESH` go in that `env` only for a task that needs an isolated data root, as a reviewed configuration change. Launching through `npx -y bladebro mcp` instead pulls the package at launch, which counts as an install and needs an operator yes.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/../mcp-servers/bladebro-mcp/README.md:57:Each MCP server process owns one Bladebro data root. Parallel isolated sessions need one process per `BLADE_HOME` or `BLADE_FRESH=1`. A second manual for that purpose is a configuration change the operator approves, and none is registered.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PBqSgEeLcX9wygWmv7xP8K","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
