{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMA6A1KFETnP4ZynZXYe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GdCjfPG6TgpDSxNxK7oCFv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; H=.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook; sed -n 30,72p $H/real-browser/attach-mode-reads.md | cut -c1-330","description":"Read BB-015 command sequence"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2183,"cache_read_input_tokens":225591,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2183},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:55:29.381Z","request_id":"<redacted>","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GdCjfPG6TgpDSxNxK7oCFv":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; H=.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook; sed -n 30,72p $H/real-browser/attach-mode-reads.md | cut -c1-330","description":"Read BB-015 command sequence"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GdCjfPG6TgpDSxNxK7oCFv","type":"tool_result","content":"- Expected execution process: the operator confirms the browser, the target site and a browser restart. Run the commands in order from the repository root on macOS, read each output and exit status, then judge them against the pass/fail criteria.\n- Expected signals: the debug port answers with a browser version, each read returns `ok: true` and exits 0, and the eval reports a signed-in page rather than a sign-in page\n- Desired user-visible outcome: Bladebro reads the signed-in site through the operator's own browser.\n- Pass/fail: PASS if the port answers and all three reads succeed on the signed-in page. FAIL if the port stays closed, any read errors or the site shows its sign-in page. Record it without a retry, then close the port.\n\n---\n\n## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n\n### Prompt\n\n- Prompt: `Attach Bladebro to my running browser and read the site I confirmed, without clicking or typing anything.`\n\n### Commands\n\n1. Quit the browser, then start it with a fixed debug port: `open -a <browser app> --args --remote-debugging-port=9333`\n2. `curl -s <url>\n3. `bladebro see content <target URL> --port 9333 --json`\n4. `bladebro see model --port 9333 --json`\n5. `bladebro act eval \"'host-match ' + (location.hostname === new URL('<target URL>').hostname) + ' sign-in ' + /sign ?in|log ?in/i.test(document.title)\" --port 9333 --json`\n6. Quit the browser, confirm `curl -s <url> gets no answer, then start the browser normally.\n\n### Expected\n\n- A `\"Browser\"` line from the debug port\n- The page text and a ref list for the target site\n- The eval result `host-match true sign-in false`: the tab is on the target and its title is not a sign-in page\n\n### Evidence\n\nEvery output and exit status. Page text, hostnames, account names, workspace names and cookie values are never quoted in the record, because on a site with one subdomain per customer the hostname is the workspace name. The record keeps the exit status, the `ok` field and the two eval booleans only.\n\n### Pass / Fail\n\n- **Pass**: the port answers and all three reads succeed on the signed-in page.\n- **Fail**: the port stays closed, any read errors or the site shows its sign-in page. Record it without a retry, then close the port.\n\n### Failure Triage\n\n1. No answer on the port means the browser was still running when it was started again. Quit it fully and repeat step 1.\n2. A sign-in page means the running browser holds no session for the site. That is a FAIL of the precondition, not of Bladebro.\n3. While the port is open any local process can drive the signed-in browser. Close it as soon as the reads finish.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:55:30.598Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- Expected execution process: the operator confirms the browser, the target site and a browser restart. Run the commands in order from the repository root on macOS, read each output and exit status, then judge them against the pass/fail criteria.\n- Expected signals: the debug port answers with a browser version, each read returns `ok: true` and exits 0, and the eval reports a signed-in page rather than a sign-in page\n- Desired user-visible outcome: Bladebro reads the signed-in site through the operator's own browser.\n- Pass/fail: PASS if the port answers and all three reads succeed on the signed-in page. FAIL if the port stays closed, any read errors or the site shows its sign-in page. Record it without a retry, then close the port.\n\n---\n\n## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n\n### Prompt\n\n- Prompt: `Attach Bladebro to my running browser and read the site I confirmed, without clicking or typing anything.`\n\n### Commands\n\n1. Quit the browser, then start it with a fixed debug port: `open -a <browser app> --args --remote-debugging-port=9333`\n2. `curl -s <url>\n3. `bladebro see content <target URL> --port 9333 --json`\n4. `bladebro see model --port 9333 --json`\n5. `bladebro act eval \"'host-match ' + (location.hostname === new URL('<target URL>').hostname) + ' sign-in ' + /sign ?in|log ?in/i.test(document.title)\" --port 9333 --json`\n6. Quit the browser, confirm `curl -s <url> gets no answer, then start the browser normally.\n\n### Expected\n\n- A `\"Browser\"` line from the debug port\n- The page text and a ref list for the target site\n- The eval result `host-match true sign-in false`: the tab is on the target and its title is not a sign-in page\n\n### Evidence\n\nEvery output and exit status. Page text, hostnames, account names, workspace names and cookie values are never quoted in the record, because on a site with one subdomain per customer the hostname is the workspace name. The record keeps the exit status, the `ok` field and the two eval booleans only.\n\n### Pass / Fail\n\n- **Pass**: the port answers and all three reads succeed on the signed-in page.\n- **Fail**: the port stays closed, any read errors or the site shows its sign-in page. Record it without a retry, then close the port.\n\n### Failure Triage\n\n1. No answer on the port means the browser was still running when it was started again. Quit it fully and repeat step 1.\n2. A sign-in page means the running browser holds no session for the site. That is a FAIL of the precondition, not of Bladebro.\n3. While the port is open any local process can drive the signed-in browser. Close it as soon as the reads finish.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GdCjfPG6TgpDSxNxK7oCFv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
