{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMAWLsq8ZCHyc5HoGziF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The opus-2 lineage finished all 7 iterations and stopped at the iteration cap. Its verdict is **FAIL**, but no finding is P0 or P1. The FAIL comes only from two required stop gates that failed.\n\n- **Coverage gate (genuine):** the two required traceability checks, spec against code and checklist evidence, ended `partial` because the review found real drift.\n- **Scope gate (a citation slip):** one finding (O2-I3-P2-003) cites a `results.csv` file that isn't in the scope list. The same problem is stated in an in-scope file, `008-live-runs-and-playbook-fixes/implementation-summary.md:144`. Iteration records are write-once, so I couldn't re-point the citation. If the merge re-anchors it there, this gate clears.\n\nLeaving the gates aside, the result would be PASS with 9 advisories.\n\n**Goal criteria checked live:**\n- Parent criteria 2, 3 and 5 hold: the hub lists 3 modes and `mcp-tooling` 6, the stale-path search finds nothing, and both routing stages pick the right mode for one prompt per mode.\n- All 14 router test cases pass, including the 403 Forbidden fix from the last review.\n- Phase 003's criteria and phase 008's PASS/FAIL tallies hold.\n- Criteria 1, 4, 6 and 7 were not re-run: they need `validate.sh` or live browser sessions, which the lineage's write limits rule out.\n\n**The 9 advisories (all P2):**\n1. \"attach to my own chrome\" routes to Chrome DevTools, but `SKILL.md:30` says Bladebro owns attaching to the user's browser.\n2. The Bladebro installer runs npm install scripts before its digest check (`install.sh:111`), and the npm launcher itself is never verified.\n3. Every completion box in the 003 and 004 goal files is unchecked, though both phases are complete and the criteria hold.\n4. The parent spec still has a TBD handoff row from 006 to 007 (`spec.md:146`) and names a branch that was removed.\n5. The live playbook verdicts point to evidence files that were never kept. Phase 008 already lists this as a known limitation.\n6. Phase 005's REQ-009 still reproduces: \"set that aside and fix the failing unit test\" returns the hub at 0.82, and no later phase owns the fix.\n7. The Aside docs still teach `page.on(...)` and `page.context()`, which the live run showed fail on the pinned Aside version (`SKILL.md:147`, `README.md:189`, the feature catalog).\n8. bdg installs from the floating `@alpha` tag, while about 10 docs describe bdg 0.6.10 behaviour.\n9. Bladebro scenario BB-015 starts the user's browser with a debug port, which branded Chrome 136+ refuses. Its troubleshooting step blames the wrong cause.\n\n**Containment:** everything this lineage wrote is inside `review/lineages/opus-2`, and every state row went through the append gateway. The skill advisor's shared database files in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/` changed during the run. My read-only advisor calls may have caused that, so the report records it as a containment conflict and leaves the files alone. The lineage lock is released. I skipped the save phase (`generate-context.js`) and git staging because the dispatch forbids both.\n\nNothing here is yours to do now; the fan-out merge reads this lineage next.\n\nFiles are in `specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-2`:\n- review-report.md\n- deep-review-findings-registry.json\n- deep-review-dashboard.md\n- resource-map.md\n- iterations/iteration-001.md … iteration-007.md\n- deltas/iter-001.jsonl … iter-007.jsonl\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:opus-2"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1031,"cache_read_input_tokens":273113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1031},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"i